// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`the milestone check sees each task’s criteria > checkPrompt lists them with ticks and reasons, and fails on unexplained gaps 1`] = `
"Every task of milestone “Network” is finished. Check its pass criteria for real, one by one:
1. Reconnects within 5 s

Its tasks, each with its acceptance criteria as its brief has them (ticked, deferred or not done with a reason):
- KLD-52 “Connection errors” (in review, PR #12 open, branch klaud/kld-52)
  - [x] Errors say why
  - [ ] The network e2e passes — deferred: suites run at the end of the plan
  - [ ] Banner goes away (not ticked, no reason)
- KLD-53 “Copy pass” (in review)
  - [ ] Words reviewed — not done: mia is away
- later “Not started” (in review)
  - [ ] Has a test (not ticked, no reason)

Read their briefs (task_get), handoffs, proof and diffs.
A criterion neither ticked nor explained is a gap: fail the milestone on it, unless you check it is true and tick it
(task_brief_edit with the task's key). A "not done" one: say whether the milestone can pass without it.
A "deferred" one is checked again at the end of the plan: don't fail on it now.

This plan runs its test suites only at the end: don't run them for this check. Check by reading the code, the diffs, the tests the tasks wrote and their typecheck.
Then call plan_gate with pass or fail and notes that say,
per criterion, what you checked and found. On pass, the plan moves on by itself.
If it fails, add the fix tasks with plan_update.
Always end your turn with plan_gate, never by asking the user how to go on: what you couldn't check (a command
that fails, a tool that isn't there) goes in the notes, and fails the check when nothing else proves it."
`;

exports[`the milestone check sees each task’s criteria > the final check lists every deferred item and requires each to be settled 1`] = `
"Every task of milestone “Wrap up” is finished. Check its pass criteria for real, one by one:
(It has none of its own: check its tasks' acceptance criteria below.)

Its tasks, each with its acceptance criteria as its brief has them (ticked, deferred or not done with a reason):
- KLD-60 “Full suite” (in review)
  - [x] Everything passes

Read their briefs (task_get), handoffs, proof and diffs.
A criterion neither ticked nor explained is a gap: fail the milestone on it, unless you check it is true and tick it
(task_brief_edit with the task's key). A "not done" one: say whether the milestone can pass without it.

This is the plan's final check: every criterion deferred along the way must be settled now, against the full suite run:
- KLD-52: The network e2e passes (deferred: suites run at the end of the plan)
For each one: true on the combined work, tick it ("- [x]", task_brief_edit with that key); not true, fail the
check and add a fix task for it with plan_update (name the criterion in its goal). Don't pass while one is still deferred.

This is the final step: run every test now, once, on the plan's combined work: typecheck, the full unit suite and the e2e.
Combine the tasks' branches in one temporary worktree (git worktree add --detach, then merge each branch), run there, and remove it after.
Run the Mac e2e with \`npm run e2e\` in packages/mac: one e2e runs at a time on this Mac (it waits, saying whose run it waits for), with its own port and demo home, and stops everything it started when it ends.
A failure that looks like load (a timeout, "did not start", a flaky wait while the Mac is busy: see \`uptime\`) counts only if it fails again when re-run once, alone.
Then call plan_gate with pass or fail and notes that say,
per criterion, what you checked and found. On pass, the plan moves on by itself.
If it fails, add the fix tasks with plan_update.
Always end your turn with plan_gate, never by asking the user how to go on: what you couldn't check (a command
that fails, a tool that isn't there) goes in the notes, and fails the check when nothing else proves it."
`;
